  "notes": "USAGE: {何|なに}も is always used with negative verb forms to mean \"nothing\" or \"not anything.\" It cannot be used in affirmative sentences.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{何|なに}も{食|た}べない (to not eat anything)\n・{何|なに}も{言|い}わない (to not say anything)\n・{何|なに}も{知|し}らない (to not know anything)\n・{何|なに}もない (there's nothing)\n・{何|なに}も〜なくてもいい (there's no need to...)\n\nCONTRAST:\n・{何|なに}か (something - affirmative)\n・{何|なに}も (nothing - negative)",
